Subject: Please backport d54601f21faf and cfa67a1dbfd9 (btusb: ASUS QCA Rome IDs) to stable

Hello,

please consider these two commits, in this order, for linux-7.3.y,
linux-6.18.y, linux-6.12.y, linux-6.6.y, linux-6.1.y, linux-5.15.y and
linux-5.10.y:

  d54601f21faf ("Bluetooth: btusb: add ASUS 0b05:1868 to QCA Rome
  quirks")
  cfa67a1dbfd9 ("Bluetooth: btusb: add ASUS 0b05:1825 to QCA Rome
  quirks")

Both are in mainline since v7.4-rc1 and carry no Cc: stable tag. They
add two device IDs to btusb's QCA ROME entries. Without an entry these
ASUS controllers match only the generic Bluetooth class entry,
btusb_setup_qca() never runs, and they stay on their ROM firmware;
both commit messages report repeated "unexpected event for opcode
0x2005" during LE scanning, which the entry stops. I do not have these
devices; the runtime results are the authors'.

On 2026-11-22 neither commit was in any of the seven trees or in their
stable queues, and both applied, in this order, to each tree's tip of
that day (7.3.5, 6.18.64, 6.12.118, 6.6.162, 6.1.192, 5.15.225,
5.10.274); cfa67a1dbfd9's context is the line d54601f21faf adds. On
2026-11-14, on that day's tips, btusb.o built with both commits with
no new warning (x86_64 defconfig, BT=m, BT_HCIBTUSB=m, W=1; on 6.6.y
the W=1 build stops on four btmtk.h errors with or without them).

Thank you,
Iaroslav Voitovych
